--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, B1 (streaming slab pass) §8: the slab passes of `axisPipe` on `GI` arrays
--
--   The three IL slab passes, on `gflat` arrays (`post` `GI` entries = `m = 2 post` integers per slab):
--
--   * **`slabId_runs`** (passes 3, 5: `h = fun _ z => z`; control `ctlOf n n' src (fun _ => 0)`),
--   * **`slabSc_runs`** (pass 1: `h = selH p P`; control `ctlOf n n' src (fun _ => 2^(P-p-1))`),
--   * **`slabOut_runs`** (pass 7: `h = outH p P s t α` on `zip Y Y₂`, source `some l`; control
--     `ctlOf N N some argO` with `argO l = d̃_l` for `l < s`, else `0`; the two arrays on stacks
--     `0` and `rZ`; constants `2^(P-p)`, `2^p` on `rK1`, `rK2`; multiplication `MulOK pM`).
--
--   Each takes the skeleton inputs (`rC` = `flatC cs ++ RC`, `rACC = []`, `rNB = pre`, `rNC = |cs|`,
--   `rM = 2 post`, `rTOT = pre · n' · 2 post`, the `rptX` counters empty) and leaves
--   `gflat (slabPass …) ++ l` on stack `0`, everything else unchanged. The cost is `passC …`;
--   with `passC_le` and `|cs| ≤ n + n'` (`length_ctlOf_le`) it is, per block,
--   `O((n + n' + 1) (post + 1) (cu + Ba + 1))` with `cu = O(Bu + 1)` (identity),
--   `O(Bu + P + 1)` (scale), `O(cU (Bu + Ba + 2) + P)` (output: one multiplication per entry).
